Replace libs/telemetry with a no-op implementation.

opentelemetry 0.91.1 (+ client-ocurl, client-cohttp-eio, logs), ambient-context
and curl are not available in the conda-forge ocaml 5.4 stack. All .ml files in
libs/telemetry are rewritten as no-ops satisfying the existing .mli files.
Only Telemetry.mli (scope / user_data are now concrete local types instead of
Opentelemetry.Span.t / Opentelemetry.value) and Logging.mli (attributes use
Telemetry.user_data) are touched; all consumers compile unchanged.
eio and eio.unix are added to the libraries because Telemetry.mli mentions
Eio types (previously pulled in transitively by opentelemetry-client-cohttp-eio).
Tracing.mli, Ometrics.mli, ppx/ and Log_telemetry/Telemetry_commons are unchanged.

